&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;At Modulr, we&#39;re committed to building a diverse, equitable and inclusive culture where everyone feels they belong and can bring their whole self to work. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds as we believe it&#39;s the right thing for our people, our business, and the community we operate in.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:80,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:100}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;By submitting your CV, you consent to us using your personal data to assess your application, contact you, or share your CV with relevant hiring managers. You can request removal of your data at any time by emailing peopleops@modulrfinance.com - though this will withdraw you from consideration for the role.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:80,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:100}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Corporate Onboarding Associate&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Old Street, London (In office 4 days)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you someone who thrives on curiosity, loves experimentation, and constantly seeks&amp;nbsp;innovative ways to solve problems?&lt;br&gt;Do you want to be hands-on in embedded payments, while continuously learning and&amp;nbsp;developing in a dynamic environment?&lt;br&gt;Do you want to play an important role in one of Europe’s fastest-growing fintech companies?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;If the answer is yes, we’d love to connect with you!&amp;nbsp;We’re looking to hire passionate, talented individuals to join Modulr, one of the fastest-growing payments businesses in the UK and Europe. This role will focus on leading and managing CDD (Customer Due Diligence) and Compliance Assessments for our clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Role:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Corporate Onboarding Associate, you’ll play a pivotal role in managing and executing CDD &amp;amp; Compliance Assessments for our clients. You’ll be part of our First Line Operations function, responsible for mitigating risks related to our services as an Electronic Money Institution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your primary focus will be on Anti-Money Laundering (AML), Counter-Terrorist Financing (CTF), and Sanctions control, while also ensuring compliance with broader business objectives such as proposition and FCA Consumer Duty. Specifically, this role operates in line with UK regulatory requirements, including the Money Laundering Regulations 2017, JMLSG Guidance, and FCA expectations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Given the ever-evolving regulatory landscape, we’re looking for someone with a sharp, inquisitive mindset, ready to dive deep into compliance and regulatory matters. In this growing team, you’ll have the opportunity to shape and implement best practices for a market-leading compliance function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client Risk Assessments: &lt;/strong&gt;Perform detailed risk assessments for corporate clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Corporate Onboarding &amp;amp; CDD: &lt;/strong&gt;Execute Customer Due Diligence, including Simplified and Enhanced Due Diligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Engagement: &lt;/strong&gt;Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders to ensure compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PEP &amp;amp; Sanction Screening: &lt;/strong&gt;Screen clients for Politically Exposed Persons and Sanctioned Individuals, including screening against UK financial sanctions lists administered by the Office of Financial Sanctions Implementation (OFSI) and HM Treasury.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Policy Review: &lt;/strong&gt;Review and recommend changes to compliance policies and procedures to align with Modulr’s regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal Corporate Onboarding Associate will thrive in a fast-paced, scaling environment and be comfortable with change and ambiguity. You bring hands-on experience in compliance and onboarding, with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–5 years of relevant experience in Customer Due Diligence (CDD), KYB, or Audit roles&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to identify compliance issues through analytical review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in a regulated financial services environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ICA (International Compliance Association) qualification in AML, KYC, or Compliance is desirable but not essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with EU/Dutch financial crime frameworks (Wwft, Sanctiewet 1970) or broader EU AML Directives (AMLD4/5/6) is desirable, given Modulr’s cross-border operations across the UK and Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Knowledge: &lt;/strong&gt;Solid understanding of UK financial crime regulations, including the Money Laundering Regulations 2017 (MLR 2017), JMLSG Guidance, Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 (POCA), Terrorism Act 2000, and FCA financial crime rules (SYSC 6), ensuring effective risk mitigation and collaboration with the second-line team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience in a compliance or onboarding role within financial services, particularly in Corporate Client Due Diligence (KYB) and AML procedures across various sectors or jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;Skilled at analysing data to identify patterns, risks, or anomalies—particularly in onboarding and audit processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attention to Detail: &lt;/strong&gt;Accurate and thorough in handling compliance documentation, reporting, and identifying areas of risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Collaboration: &lt;/strong&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage confidently with clients and internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ethical Judgement &amp;amp; Integrity: &lt;/strong&gt;High ethical standards with a strong sense of responsibility and confidentiality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organisation &amp;amp; Ownership: &lt;/strong&gt;Ability to manage competing tasks and projects effectively, taking ownership of compliance processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability &amp;amp; Problem Solving: &lt;/strong&gt;Flexible in the face of regulatory or operational change, and proactive in finding solutions.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Share Options&lt;/strong&gt; – We offer a Company Share Option Plan (CSOP), giving you the opportunity to benefit from any increase in share value in the event of a sale, merger, or flotation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus&lt;/strong&gt; – Our annual discretionary bonus, paid in May for the previous year, is based on both company and individual performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible benefits&lt;/strong&gt; – £1,000 to spend on benefits to suit you, including private medical insurance, gym membership, dental etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellbeing app&lt;/strong&gt; – confidential, on-demand access to therapy, coaching, counselling, management training or mindfulness sessions with accredited professionals, with company-funded hours and top-up options available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holidays&lt;/strong&gt; – 33 days annual leave (including bank holidays) plus your birthday off. In the UK, Christmas Day, Boxing Day, and New Year&#39;s Day are fixed holidays. You can choose the remaining days to suit your personal schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning opportunities&lt;/strong&gt; – Our two-day onboarding programme, ModStart, helps equip you for success. Learning doesn&#39;t stop there; we&#39;ll continue to support your development through various channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company-Wide Events&lt;/strong&gt; – Participate in collaborative and engaging events with colleagues across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bike to work / E-bike scheme&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ModInclusion&lt;br&gt;We believe that a diverse and inclusive culture is vital to our success. We encourage applications from individuals of diverse backgrounds, ensuring that everyone at Modulr feels they belong and can bring their authentic selves to work.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;London (Old Street)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-time&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4 days/week in office&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You own Modulr’s voice and how we show day to day on owned and earned online channels, from a fast-moving LinkedIn trend in the morning to a considered pitch to an industry influencer in the afternoon.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work closely with and learn from the Head of PR and Communications and the wider marketing team, on fast-moving campaigns and projects that make a real impact to the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You get to build something genuinely new for us: how Modulr engages with brands and partners to help us improve AI visibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Modulr&amp;nbsp;is the&amp;nbsp;payments&amp;nbsp;automation platform that streamlines money movement with accuracy,&amp;nbsp;control&amp;nbsp;and reliability – built to scale. We process more than 200m transactions and over £180bn in payment value on an&amp;nbsp;annualised&amp;nbsp;basis, and&amp;nbsp;we’re&amp;nbsp;trusted by over 6,000 businesses from fast-growing SMEs to global enterprises.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We automate how money moves into and out of a business (payroll, supplier payments, spend management and payment collection) through a single platform, connected to the accounting and payroll systems finance teams already use, and underpinned by principal memberships of Visa and Mastercard and direct access to central bank infrastructure.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a regulated payments provider with over a decade of experience,&amp;nbsp;we’re&amp;nbsp;the platform finance teams&amp;nbsp;trust&amp;nbsp;to run mission-critical operations.&amp;nbsp;Modulr&amp;nbsp;is backed by PayPal, FIS, General Atlantic, Blenheim&amp;nbsp;Chalcot, Frog&amp;nbsp;Capital&amp;nbsp;and Highland Europe, with over 400 employees across London, Edinburgh,&amp;nbsp;Amsterdam&amp;nbsp;and Mumbai.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find out more about us on our&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;website&lt;/u&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the day-to-day running of Modulr’s social media presence and digital PR outreach, working closely with the Head of PR and Communications to build a consistent, credible and engaging brand voice across our owned channels and in online/digital earned media.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role for someone who deeply understands social media trends shaping B2B, payments, and fintech conversations online, and how to join these conversations in an authentic way. You will also take the lead on a newer piece of the puzzle: identifying and creating campaigns around brands and platforms we should work with to improve AI visibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead on strategy and calendars for our social media channels, what platforms we should engage with and wen, content creating, influencer relationship building, and tracks what is working, reporting into the Head of PR and Communications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Social Media Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Content Creation – &lt;/strong&gt;Plan, write and schedule creative, platform-tailored content (copy, images, short-form video, and graphics) across channels including LinkedIn, Instagram, TikTok, and X.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community Management – &lt;/strong&gt;Monitor our channels, respond to comments and direct messages proactively, and foster healthy, active two-way conversations with our followers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trend Tracking – &lt;/strong&gt;Keep a pulse on cultural moments, trending audio, and industry news so we can join relevant online conversations, including reactive and newsjacking content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scheduling &amp;amp; Calendars – &lt;/strong&gt;Own and maintain the active social media content calendar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Digital PR &amp;amp; Outreach&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Campaign Support – &lt;/strong&gt;Help plan and execute end-to-end digital PR campaigns, including press releases, data-led studies, and reactive commentary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Media Relations – &lt;/strong&gt;Build and maintain targeted media lists and pitch journalists, bloggers, and relevant trade publications, using databases such as Muck Rack or Roxhill.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influencer &amp;amp; Partner Collaboration – &lt;/strong&gt;Liaise with micro-influencers, brand advocates, and partners to amplify campaigns and extend our reach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coverage Monitoring – &lt;/strong&gt;Track, clip and report on online brand mentions, features, and sentiment shifts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytics &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Tracking – &lt;/strong&gt;Monitor key metrics, including reach, engagement, referral traffic, and share of voice, using social and PR analytics tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting – &lt;/strong&gt;Compile weekly and monthly reports with actionable insights that refine future content and outreach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Visibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; –&lt;/strong&gt; identify the brands and platforms worth working with to improve AI visibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of hands-on experience in social media, digital PR/marketing, journalism, public relations, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An exceptional writer who can shift tone for the audience in front of you, from a snappy social caption to a professional media or influencer pitch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with all the major social platforms, including LinkedIn, Instagram, TikTok, X, and YouTube, and how each one actually works.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable with social scheduling and analytics tools such as Hubsot, Hootsuite, or Sprout Social, and basic design tools such as Canva, Figma, or Adobe Creative Suite. Familiarity with media monitoring tools like Meltwater or Cision is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A working understanding of SEO, Google Analytics, and native social analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are creative and quick-thinking, able to come up with fresh content fast and respond to online trends as they happen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organised and can juggle multiple tasks, campaigns, and deadlines in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a confident communicator who enjoys building relationships with media/influencer contacts and online communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications such as CIM, CIPR, HubSpot, or Meta Blueprint are advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Share Options – &lt;/strong&gt;We offer a Company Share Option Plan (CSOP), giving you the opportunity to benefit from any increase in share value in the event of a sale, merger, or flotation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus – &lt;/strong&gt;Our annual discretionary bonus, paid in May for the previous year, is based on both company and individual performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible benefits – &lt;/strong&gt;£1,000 to spend on benefits to suit you, including private medical insurance, gym membership and dental.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellbeing app – &lt;/strong&gt;confidential, on-demand access to therapy, coaching, counselling, management training or mindfulness sessions with accredited professionals, with company-funded hours and top-up options available.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holidays – &lt;/strong&gt;33 days annual leave (including bank holidays) plus your birthday off. In the UK, Christmas Day, Boxing Day and New Year’s Day are fixed holidays. You can choose the remaining days to suit your personal schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning opportunities – &lt;/strong&gt;Our two-day onboarding programme, ModStart, helps equip you for success. Learning does not stop there; we will continue to support your development through various channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company-Wide Events – &lt;/strong&gt;Participate in collaborative and engaging events with colleagues across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bike to work / E-bike scheme&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ModInclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Modulr, we are committed to building a diverse, equitable and inclusive culture where everyone feels they belong and can bring their whole self to work. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds as we believe it is the right thing for our people, our business, and the community we operate in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;By submitting your CV, you consent to us using your personal data to assess your application, contact you, or share your CV with relevant hiring managers. You can request removal of your data at any time by emailing peopleops@modulrfinance.com, though this will withdraw you from consideration for the role.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finance Transformation Manager&lt;br&gt;Location: Mumbai&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do you have a background in Finance transformation, systems change and project delivery?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do you want to own Finance systems and change end-to-end in a fast-scaling embedded payments business?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do you want the opportunity to shape how a modern Finance function runs across systems, controls and processes?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If so, we would love to connect and collaborate!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Modulr is the payments automation platform that streamlines money movement with accuracy, control and reliability — built to scale. We process more than 200m transactions and over £180bn in payment value on an annualised basis, and we’re trusted by over 6,000 businesses from fast-growing SMEs to global enterprises.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We automate how money moves into and out of a business — payroll, supplier payments, spend management and payment collection — through a single platform, connected to the accounting and payroll systems finance teams already use and underpinned by principal memberships of Visa and Mastercard and direct access to central bank infrastructure.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a regulated payments provider with over a decade of experience, we’re the platform finance teams trust to run mission-critical operations. Modulr is backed by PayPal, FIS, General Atlantic, Blenheim Chalcot, Frog Capital and Highland Europe, with over 400 employees across London, Edinburgh, Amsterdam, Mumbai and Pune.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead, govern and deliver Finance transformation, systems change and operational improvement across Modulr&#39;s Finance function. You will ensure Finance has scalable, controlled and well-documented processes, effective systems, clear ownership and robust project governance, working across Financial Control, FP&amp;amp;A, Finance Operations, Product, Technology, People, Legal, Risk, Compliance, external advisers and system vendors. The role reports into the Director of Financial Control and supports the CFO and wider Finance leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibility&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Finance transformation and continuous improvement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Finance transformation initiatives across Financial Control, FP&amp;amp;A, Finance Operations, Payroll, Billing and Treasury.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to simplify, standardise, automate and strengthen Finance processes, facilitating workshops to move from current to future state.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop workplans and implementation approaches that are practical, controlled and capable of being adopted by the relevant teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own NetSuite and Finance systems change&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the Finance-side owner for NetSuite change requirements, enhancements and adoption - scoping, prioritising, testing and coordinating changes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Finance requirements for approvals, cost centres, entities, country packs, billing logic, reporting, integration and data integrity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate UAT, release planning, defect tracking and Finance sign-off, working with Coefficient, Oracle and Technology teams to resolve issues.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support decisions on licenses, add-ons, system capability and renewals, ensuring NetSuite remains a reliable source of truth, alongside tools such as Web expenses and TravelPerk.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Govern the Finance project portfolio&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a structured view of Finance initiatives, priorities, owners, dependencies and status.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain RAID logs, action trackers and decision logs, giving visibility of delivery risks, blockers and decision points.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support prioritisation with Finance leadership and prepare concise updates for finance leadership and cross-functional stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver projects end-to-end&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply a structured, control-led project framework from discovery and problem definition through scope, planning and governance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead solution design workshops and translate Finance requirements into clear specifications for Technology, vendors and implementation partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate UAT, testing and validation, then go-live readiness, change readiness and controlled handover into BAU.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run post-implementation reviews to confirm benefits, capture lessons learned and close residual risks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support new entity, jurisdiction and regulatory change&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead or support Finance readiness for new entities and jurisdictional expansion - payroll, bank accounts, NetSuite setup, tax, transfer pricing and regulatory reporting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with external advisers including KPMG, Deloitte and other specialists, and support tax, regulatory and compliance evidence gathering.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Finance impacts are identified, tracked and delivered in a controlled way, with handover to BAU once stable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage vendors, advisers and third parties&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage day-to-day Finance engagement with key vendors and external advisers, coordinating requests, requirements, actions and escalations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge unclear scope, costs, delays or outputs, keeping vendor activity aligned to Finance timelines, priorities and controls.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support commercial awareness around licences, implementation costs, support arrangements and renewals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embed controls, auditability and risk management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed control considerations into Finance change from the design stage - approvals, evidence, segregation of duties, documentation and audit trails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify operational, financial, regulatory and data risks, and maintain risk and issue logs with owners, mitigations and escalation routes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audit evidence gathering and walkthroughs for areas impacted by Finance change.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead stakeholders and build capability&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships across Finance, Product, Technology, People, Legal, Risk, Compliance and external partners, communicating complex issues in a concise, decision-focused way.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support senior leaders with updates, analysis, options, risks and recommendations, and facilitate alignment where ownership spans functions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide coaching and practical support to Finance colleagues, create training materials and system guidance, and promote consistent project, documentation and risk disciplines.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Person Specification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident using AI tools to draft documentation, analyse information, map processes and improve productivity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience delivering Finance change, transformation and systems projects end-to-end - ideally involving an ERP such as NetSuite - from discovery through to post-implementation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management discipline across scope, planning, RAID governance, UAT, handover and benefits realisation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid Finance process knowledge across R2R, P2P, and O2C with a strong controls, audit and documentation mindset.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management - able to translate Finance needs for technical, operational and vendor teams and communicate concisely to senior leaders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of new entity or multi-jurisdiction setup and working with external advisers (e.g. KPMG, Deloitte, tax and payroll providers).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a regulated financial services or fintech environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer You &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Share Options&lt;/strong&gt; – We offer a Company Share Option Plan (CSOP), giving you the opportunity to benefit from any increase in share value in the event of a sale, merger, or flotation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus &lt;/strong&gt;– Our annual discretionary bonus, paid in May for the previous year, is based on both company and individual performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insurance Coverage&lt;/strong&gt; – Comprehensive medical, life, and accident insurance provided to support you and your family&#39;s wellbeing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holidays &amp;amp; Leave&lt;/strong&gt; – A generous annual leave allowance, your birthday off, and menstrual leave for female employees, with the flexibility to choose days to suit your personal schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development&lt;/strong&gt; – Our onboarding programme, ModStart, equips you for success. Learning doesn&#39;t stop there; we&#39;ll continue to support your development through various channels and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mental Health, Wellbeing &amp;amp; Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt; – Access to accredited therapists, coaches, counsellors, management training, and mindfulness sessions with company-funded hours and flexible top-up options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company-Wide Events&lt;/strong&gt; – Participate in collaborative and engaging events with colleagues across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ModInclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Modulr, we’re committed to building a diverse, equitable and inclusive culture where everyone feels they belong and can bring their whole self to work. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds as we believe it’s the right thing for our people, our business, and the community we operate in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

