&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Marketing &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;London&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-time &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In office 4 days/week&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are you looking for a high-ownership role defining how a fast-growing payments automation platform shows up in its highest-value industries?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can you balance rigor with pace, and strategy with hands-on craft?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If so, we would love to hear from you!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Modulr is the payments automation platform that streamlines money movement with accuracy, control and reliability – built to scale. We process more than 200m transactions and over £180bn in payment value on an annualised basis, and we&#39;re trusted by over 6,000 businesses from fast-growing SMEs to global enterprises.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We automate how money moves into and out of a business – payroll, supplier payments, spend management and payment collection – through a single platform, connected to the accounting and payroll systems finance teams already use and underpinned by principal memberships of Visa and Mastercard and direct access to central bank infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a regulated payments provider with over a decade of experience, we&#39;re the platform finance teams trust to run mission-critical operations. Modulr is backed by PayPal, FIS, General Atlantic, Blenheim Chalcot, Frog Capital and Highland Europe, with over 400 employees across London, Edinburgh, Amsterdam and Mumbai.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find out more about us on our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.modulrfinance.com/&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.modulrfinance.com/life-at-modulr&quot;&gt;careers site&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Positioning &amp;amp; Narrative&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define sharp, differentiated positioning for Modulr&#39;s Travel and Lending solutions – grounded in deep customer insight, competitive understanding and a clear point of view on where we win.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate a technically rich payments platform into clear, compelling messaging that resonates with finance, operations and commercial buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a high bar for narrative consistency and storytelling craft across every vertical touchpoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vertical Go-to-Market&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a scalable model for how Modulr enters, expands and doubles down in industry verticals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product on roadmap prioritisation, shaping what gets built and how it reaches the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Enablement &amp;amp; Revenue Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arm the commercial team with assets that really move deals – pitches, sales decks, one-pagers, demo narratives, competitive battlecards and win stories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the team on driving measurable improvements in pipeline quality, win rates and deal velocity in your verticals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Sales leaders to translate customer insights into messaging and enablement that reflects how buyers really make decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market &amp;amp; Customer Intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a deep understanding of each vertical – buyer personas, buyer journeys, regulatory context, competitive landscape and unmet needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesise customer conversations, win/loss and usage data into actionable insights that shape product, marketing and sales decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become the person leaders across Modulr turn to when they need a clear read on a vertical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Launches &amp;amp; Campaigns&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own launch plans for new vertical propositions and product updates – from positioning to activation across web, events, press and demand generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Brand, Content and Demand Generation to turn vertical narratives into campaigns that build category authority and pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the quality and consistency of vertical storytelling across the website and key growth surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience.&lt;/strong&gt; 6+ years in product marketing or product strategy in B2B SaaS, fintech or payments – with a strong track record of marketing to mid-market and enterprise buyers. Vertical or industry-led GTM experience is a significant plus; payments or fintech experience is preferred but not required for the right generalist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic thinking. &lt;/strong&gt;You form sharp points of view, work from first principles, and can turn complex, ambiguous inputs into a clear strategic direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Storytelling &amp;amp; craft. &lt;/strong&gt;An exceptional communicator who can make a technically rich product feel simple, differentiated and genuinely compelling – to finance leaders, operators and commercial teams alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial orientation. &lt;/strong&gt;You think in terms of pipeline, win rates and revenue – not just launches and assets. You partner naturally with Sales and are energised by driving commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical fluency. &lt;/strong&gt;Comfortable engaging credibly with Product and Engineering on how the platform actually works, and confident translating that into buyer value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence &amp;amp; ownership. &lt;/strong&gt;You lead cross-functionally without needing authority, push work forward through ambiguity, and elevate the quality of everyone around you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High expectations. &lt;/strong&gt;You hold a high bar on messaging precision, visual presentation and the quality of what goes out the door. You use data to make decisions, measure impact and iterate quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Share Options&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;– We offer a Company Share Option Plan (CSOP), giving you the opportunity to benefit from any increase in share value in the event of a sale, merger, or flotation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;– Our annual discretionary bonus, paid in May for the previous year, is based on both company and individual performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible benefits&lt;/strong&gt; - £1000 to spend on benefits to suit you, including private medical insurance, gym membership, dental etc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellbeing app &lt;/strong&gt;– confidential, on-demand access to therapy, coaching, counselling, management training or mindfulness sessions with accredited professionals, with company-funded hours and top-up options available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holidays &lt;/strong&gt;-&amp;nbsp;33 days annual leave (including bank holidays) plus your birthday off. In the UK, Christmas Day, Boxing Day, and New Year’s Day are fixed holidays. You can choose the remaining days to suit your personal schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning opportunities&lt;/strong&gt;- Our two-day onboarding program, ModStart, helps equip you for success. Learning doesn’t stop there; we’ll continue to support your development through various channels. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company-Wide Events&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;-&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Participate in collaborative and engaging events with colleagues across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bike to work / E-bike scheme&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ModInclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Modulr, we’re committed to building a diverse, equitable and inclusive culture where everyone feels they belong and can bring their whole self to work. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds as we believe it’s the right thing for our people, our business, and the community we operate in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your CV, you consent to us using your personal data to assess your application, contact you, or share your CV with relevant hiring managers. You can request removal of your data at any time by emailing&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:peopleops@modulrfinance.com&quot;&gt;peopleops@modulrfinance.com&lt;/a&gt; - though this will withdraw you from consideration for the role.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;•Are you curious, excited by experimentation and always looking to innovate?&lt;br&gt;•Do you want to work in embedded payments where you can keep learning and developing whilst getting hands-on experience?&lt;br&gt;•Do you want to have the opportunity to play an important role in a rapidly growing and exciting Fintech business?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If so, we would love to connect and collaborate!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want to hire ambitious, and value-adding talent into Modulr, one of the fastest growing payments businesses in the UK and Europe. Modulr is experiencing significant growth, and in this role you will work in a cross-functional team who are asked to solve a problem, rather than be handed a task to do. This is an excellent opportunity to work in a high-growth environment with a fast-paced and collaborative culture where you will have great opportunities to work on challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Modulr, our vision is a world where all businesses are powered by embedded payments. Modulr enables businesses, from SMEs to Enterprise, initially across the UK and Europe to efficiently pay-in, collect and disburse funds instantly via a range of payment schemes, accounts, and card products.&lt;br&gt;We have created an industry-leading API platform with comprehensive online tools and access, to meet the demands of daily business payments. We have two routes to market. Our Core Business Payments product allows customers in any sector to connect to us and our expanding network of accounting and payroll platforms, including Sage, Xero, BrightPay and IRIS to automate payments. Our Vertical Solutions targets a growing range of industry verticals which directly connect their IT platforms to our APIs and webhooks. We solve complex payment problems for hundreds of clients in a range of industries, including Travel, Lending, Wage Advance, and Investment &amp;amp; Wealth.&lt;br&gt;We are deeply integrated into the payment eco-system. In the UK, we are direct participants of Faster Payments and Bacs. Modulr hold settlement accounts at the Bank of England. Our payment network connectivity includes CHAPS, Open Banking, SEPA, SWIFT and account issuance in multiple currencies. We are principal issuing members of Visa and Mastercard schemes across UK and Europe.&lt;br&gt;Our regulatory permissions and governance structure are the foundations of our business. We are regulated and supervised as an Authorised Electronic Money Institution (AEMI) in the UK by the Financial Conduct Authority and in the Netherlands by De Nederlandsche Bank.&lt;br&gt;Our founding team has a wealth of experience in the payments industry and growing successful businesses. Modulr is backed by the venture arms of payments giants PayPal and FIS, as well as growth investors Blenheim Chalcot, General Atlantic, Frog Capital and Highland Europe.&lt;br&gt;Modulr now has over 400 employees spread globally across offices in London, Edinburgh, Amsterdam, Mumbai and Pune.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modulr values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;•Building the extraordinary; going that extra mile.&lt;br&gt;•Owning the opportunity; be passionate and proud of the time you invest.&lt;br&gt;•Move at pace; reach goals faster whilst supported on your career journey.&lt;br&gt;•Achieve it together, working collaboratively and being a Modulite.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Modulr we are focused on building autonomous squads that are focused on working in&lt;br&gt;the best possible way. We operate in a tribes and squad model with each area focused on&lt;br&gt;a particular growth area. Each squad is small and cross-functional. We have big ambitions and have many interesting challenges ahead.&lt;br&gt;Summary&lt;br&gt;In this role you will design, build, and evolve the next generation of Modulr’s event-driven payments platform. You’ll work across the full engineering lifecycle—from shaping technical approaches to delivering production-grade software—within a squad that values ownership, excellence, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Specific duties&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering &amp;amp; Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;•Design and develop backend services using Java (17+) or similar OO languages.&lt;br&gt;•Build and evolve microservices and distributed, event-driven components in a cloud-native environment.&lt;br&gt;•Contribute to architectural patterns that support throughput, resilience, reliability, and observability.&lt;br&gt;•Design clean, well-documented RESTful APIs and service contracts.&lt;br&gt;•Work with relational data stores, especially PostgreSQL, and contribute to data modelling.&lt;br&gt;Distributed Systems &amp;amp; Reliability&lt;br&gt;•Engineer solutions for concurrency, idempotency, fault tolerance, retries, and high availability.&lt;br&gt;•Improve system performance, reduce latency, and identify bottlenecks across services.&lt;br&gt;•Build systems with strong observability—logs, metrics, tracing—ensuring issues can be diagnosed quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality &amp;amp; Testing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;•Develop comprehensive automated tests using frameworks such as JUnit, Mockito, Cucumber.&lt;br&gt;•Participate in design and code reviews, helping raise engineering standards across the team.&lt;br&gt;•Advocate for code quality, maintainability, and long-term technical health.&lt;br&gt;DevOps, Cloud &amp;amp; Tooling&lt;br&gt;•Use and improve deployment pipelines and operational tooling (Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD, AWS services).&lt;br&gt;•Contribute to internal frameworks, shared libraries, and engineering best practices.&lt;br&gt;•Help shape the evolution of our platform toward a more flexible, modern architecture.&lt;br&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Delivery&lt;br&gt;•Work in an agile environment, contributing to planning, design discussions, and iterative delivery.&lt;br&gt;•Collaborate across squads to shape technical solutions that span multiple systems.&lt;br&gt;•Document best practices, reference architectures, and design approaches others can rely on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’re an engineer who thrives in a fast-paced, high-growth environment and enjoys solving complex, system-level problems. You bring:&lt;br&gt;•&lt;strong&gt;4+ years&lt;/strong&gt; expertise in Java or another OO language with willingness to work in Java.&lt;br&gt;•Strong understanding of OOP, design patterns, and distributed systems fundamentals.&lt;br&gt;•Experience building and operating microservices in production.&lt;br&gt;•Ability to reason about concurrency, performance, and system behaviour under load.&lt;br&gt;•Clear, proactive communication and a collaborative, team-first mindset.&lt;br&gt;•Strong analytical and problem-solving skills supported by sound engineering judgement.&lt;br&gt;•Ability to manage complexity, balance competing priorities, and deliver high-quality work.&lt;br&gt;•A growth mindset—you enjoy learning, improving, and helping others grow.&lt;br&gt;•A self-starter attitude with a passion for ownership and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ModInclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Modulr, we are working hard to build a more positive diverse and inclusive culture that helps everyone to feel they belong and can truly bring their whole self to work. Not only is it the right thing to do for everyone in the Modulr team, it’s also the right thing to do for our business, the community we operate in and attracting future talent. As part of our approach, we actively welcome applications from candidates with diverse backgrounds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Partnerships Manager, Travel&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;London&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Full-time &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In office 4 days/week&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven&amp;nbsp;track record&amp;nbsp;of sourcing and signing new partnerships in the travel payments ecosystem&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong network across travel — GDS, intermediaries, aggregators, OTAs, TMCs and travel SaaS platforms&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of embedded payments and virtual cards, and how travel platforms embed them to create value&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this sounds like you, we would love to hear from you!  &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our vision is a world where all businesses are powered by embedded payments.&amp;nbsp;Modulr&amp;nbsp;enables businesses from SMEs to enterprises, initially across the UK, Europe and the US to efficiently pay in, collect, and disburse funds instantly via a range of payment schemes, accounts, and card products. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
